{
  "instruction": "# Conditional guidance\n\nSome of this project's guidance applies CONDITIONALLY. Each entry gives a\nfragment's NAME and the PREMISE under which it applies. Load any your\ncontext does not already carry.\n\nMatch against WHAT YOU ARE ABOUT TO DO -- the next action, not the whole\nconversation behind you. Take each premise ON ITS OWN and ask whether it\ndescribes that action; you are not picking the single best match, and\nseveral premises often apply at once.\n\nWhen it is a BORDERLINE call, include it. An unnecessary fragment costs a\nlittle context; one you withhold is never learned to exist and cannot be\nasked for.\n\nSelect on the premise, not on the name. Then call the ctxloom\n`assemble_context` tool with the names you chose (the `bundles` argument)\nand follow what it returns.\n",
